      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "An 8-year-old girl suffering from hereditary spherocytosis underwent splenectomy for chronic severe anaemia. Surgery was uneventful and the patient had a good early postoperative recovery. On the third postoperative day, however, she developed severe headache with associated abnormal movements of upper limbs and nystagmus. She had a heart rate of 50\u2005bpm and a blood pressure of 180/110\u2005mm\u2005Hg. She was managed with triple antihypertensives, antiepileptics and sedatives. She recovered slowly over 2\u2005weeks and is fine at 5\u2005months follow-up."
      },
